ABOUT NU

Nu is the leading digital bank in Latin America, serving 135 million customers across Brazil, Mexico, and Colombia. The company has been leading an industry transformation by leveraging data and proprietary technology to develop innovative products and services.

Guided by its mission to fight complexity and empower people, Nu caters to customers’ complete financial journey, promoting financial access and advancement with responsible lending and transparency. The company is powered by an efficient and scalable business model that combines low cost to serve with growing returns.

Nu’s impact has been recognized in multiple awards, including Time 100 Most Influential Companies, Fast Company’s Most Innovative Companies, and Forbes World’s Best Banks.

Visit our Institutional Page https://www.nu.com/2026-en

YOU'LL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR

As a Senior Systems Engineer working in a Cloud Network platform engineering team, you're expected to:

- Have solid troubleshooting and debugging skills with a passion for working creatively and analytically in a problem-solving environment with continuous improvement;

- Have familiarity with DevOps culture;

- Have the ability to analyze complex data and develop innovative solutions;

- Validate ideas and collaborates with in-house engineers and developers to promote creative solutions;

- Have familiarity with buy vs build approaches, evaluating new products and technologies;

- Execute high-level and low-level design for connectivity patterns for cloud network environments, considering multi-account and hybrid-cloud needs;

- Have experience with system administration (familiarity with Linux OS, scripting) and Infrastructure as Code tools;

- Have coding skills or interest to learn software development;

- Have previous PCI CSS experience or a similar security standard, considering the network security aspects of it;

- Support the Cloud Network topology, including troubleshooting incidents promptly, handling network changes, and participating in problem management processes including root cause analysis, and configuration management;

- Provide a reliable and stable infrastructure via best practices, standards, simplified support models, automated processes, operational excellence, and outstanding customer satisfaction;

- Have the ability to be data-driven before committing to a solution, taking relevant aspects like stability, reliability, scalability, and costs into account;

- Effective monitoring, implement a robust control and delivery of solutions services to identify issues proactively within the agreed SLAs using different methodologies, tools, and processes;

Have the ability to document the solutions for cross-teams knowledge sharing;

 

WE ARE LOOKING FOR A PERSON WHO HAS:

 

- Bachelor's degree in Computer Engineering, Systems Analysis and Development, or a related technical field.

- CCNP certification or equivalent experience, meaning you are comfortable designing, building, implementing, maintaining, and troubleshooting complex networking infrastructures.

- 2+ years of hands-on experience in infrastructure automation and cloud computing (AWS public cloud preferred), focused on AWS networking services.

- 2+ years of experience in planning, deploying, and troubleshooting network solutions (including IP addressing planning, BGP routing, and physical devices such as firewalls, load balancers, routers, and switches).

- English proficiency, with the ability to read, write, and participate in meetings.

 

YOU'LL FIT WELL IF YOU HAVE:

 

- Leadership and a collaborative mindset-the ability to work with team members regardless of seniority level.

- Strong communication skills with both technical and non-technical audiences, a willingness to share knowledge, and openness to feedback.

- The ability to collaborate with customers when necessary to fulfill deliverables.

- Proficiency in English to facilitate clear and consistent understanding across time zones and language

At RecargaPay , we’re on a mission to deliver the best payment experience for Brazilian consumers and small businesses, by building a powerful digital ecosystem where the banked and unbanked connect, and where consumers and merchants have a one-stop shop for all their financial needs.
We serve over 10 million users and process more than USD 4 billion annually. We’ve been profitable since 2022 and operate our own credit business. We are an AI-first, 100% remote team, scaling in the rapidly changing Brazilian financial market.
Our goal? Deliver the best payment experience in Brazil for people and small businesses alike.
We value autonomy, ownership, and a bias for action. We’re looking for people who are curious, hands-on, and driven by impact, who want to solve real problems, work with strong teams, and rethink what’s possible.
If you’re ready to do your best work, at scale, with purpose, this is your place.

Responsibilities

We're looking for a Senior Product Designer who takes ownership of the end-to-end experience within their squad, combining product thinking, data analysis, and craft to deliver solutions that work for users and drive business results.
What you'll do

• Partner with PMs and engineers to define product strategy and shape experiences grounded in user needs and business goals;

• Identify improvement opportunities proactively, formulating hypotheses and designing data-driven experiments to validate them;

• Translate data-research findings and analytics into tangible product decisions;

• Use AI tools actively to accelerate concept generation, iterate faster, and improve the quality of UX writing and design decisions;

• Contribute to the Design System, maintaining and expanding it as the product evolves;

• Collaborate across the UX team, including writers, frontend engineers, and DesignOps;

• Raise the bar for design quality, with solid command of UI, usability, and interaction patterns;

• Document your process and share knowledge with the team.

Requirements

• Proven experience in Product Design, ideally within the Brazilian financial ecosystem;

• Strong grasp of the end-to-end design process, with emphasis on fast prototyping and experimentation;

• Ability to identify and prioritize opportunities, create experiments, and define success metrics collaboratively;

• Fluency with AI tools as part of the daily design workflow, not as a novelty but as a productivity and quality multiplier;

• Clear communication with cross-functional teams, especially engineering;

• Familiarity with accessibility best practices and multi-device UX;

• Organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable working in fast-paced, interdisciplinary environments;

• Ability to present and defend design decisions to senior leadership and C-level stakeholders;

• Owner mentality: business-oriented, data-driven, and accountable for results.

Benefits

• Competitive and market-aligned salary.

• Remote work - wherever you are, you’re part of the team!

• Home office allowance through a monthly deposit in the RecargaPay app.

• Health and dental plans with no co-pay.

• Life insurance.

• Flexible meal allowance (via Flash).

• TotalPass membership to take care of your health.

Diversity & Inclusion at RecargaPay

At RecargaPay , you’ll have the freedom to be who you are because we believe that diverse perspectives and experiences make us more creative and stronger. Here, everyone is welcome to express themselves authentically. We value the richness of each journey and the multiple ways of seeing the world, without distinctions of gender, race, sexual orientation, age, religion, or any other characteristic that makes us unique.
